      "problem": "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe integer $38$ \n{{field-1}}\nthe additive inverse of $26$ modulo $64$ since $38+26$ {{field-2}} $(\\text{mod}\\,64).$",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $26$ modulo $64$ is the integer $0\\le x<64$ such that\n\n$$\nx+26≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,64).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that when we add our two numbers, we get a number that is congruent to zero modulo $64:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}38+26 & ≡64 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,64) \\\\  & ≡0 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,64)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude the following:\n\nThe integer $38$ $\\text{is}$ the additive inverse of $26$ modulo $64$ since $38+26≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,64).$",
